title = Palladium
description = Palladium is a chemical element; it has the symbol Pd and atomic number 46. It is a rare and lustrous silvery-white metal discovered in 1802 by the English chemist William Hyde Wollaston. He named it after the asteroid 2 Pallas, which was itself named after the epithet of the Greek goddess Athena, acquired by her when she slew Pallas.
